(963,'surerank_site_seo_checks','a:2:{s:5:\"other\";a:3:{s:17:\"other_seo_plugins\";a:5:{s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:6:\"status\";s:7:\"success\";s:11:\"description\";a:14:{i:0;s:142:\"<img class=\"w-full h-full\" src=\"https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/other-seo-plugin-banner.webp\" alt=\"Other SEO Plugin Banner\" />\";i:1;s:29:\"<h6>SEO Plugin Conflicts</h6>\";i:2;s:221:\"SEO plugins decide how your site appears in search results by managing titles, descriptions, and structured information. They help search engines understand your content, but also make your site easier for people to find.\";i:3;s:32:\"<h6>💡 Why this matters: </h6>\";i:4;s:282:\"Having more than one SEO plugin active can create confusion. Each plugin might try to change the same things, sending mixed signals to search engines. This can affect how clearly your site appears in search results and make it harder for visitors to find what they’re looking for.\";i:5;s:40:\"<h6>✅ How to keep things smooth: </h6>\";i:6;a:1:{s:4:\"list\";a:3:{i:0;s:77:\"Use only one SEO plugin at a time to keep your settings clean and consistent.\";i:1;s:84:\"Let that plugin handle everything in one place, so there’s no overlap or conflict.\";i:2;s:85:\"Check your plugin settings regularly to make sure nothing is accidentally duplicated.\";}}i:7;s:22:\"<h6>📌 Example </h6>\";i:8;s:164:\"If two plugins try to set your homepage description differently, search engines may receive mixed information, resulting in inconsistent search results or snippets.\";i:9;s:36:\"<h6>🛠️ Where to update it </h6>\";i:10;s:115:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/other-seo-plugin-sub-image.webp\' />\";i:11;s:190:\"You can review your active plugins from your WordPress plugins page and deactivate extras. Then manage all your SEO settings from your main SEO plugin for a clear and single source of truth.\";i:12;s:33:\"<h6>🌟 How SureRank helps </h6>\";i:13;s:200:\"SureRank keeps your SEO setup simple and reliable. It explains why using a single plugin matters, helping you maintain clarity for both search engines and your visitors, without unnecessary confusion.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:41:\"No other SEO plugin detected on the site.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}s:13:\"site_tag_line\";a:5:{s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:6:\"status\";s:7:\"warning\";s:11:\"description\";a:10:{i:0;s:196:\"Your site tagline is a simple line that helps explain what your website is about. It often shows up in the browser tab, homepage, or in search snippets — depending on your theme or SEO settings.\";i:1;s:172:\"Leaving it blank, using a default message like “Just another WordPress site,” or writing something unclear doesn’t help people or search engines understand your site.\";i:2;s:28:\"<h6> Why this matters: </h6>\";i:3;s:173:\"A good tagline can instantly tell visitors what your site offers — and make it more appealing in search results. Think of it like a mini pitch that follows your site name.\";i:4;s:27:\"<h6> What you can do: </h6>\";i:5;s:88:\"Write one short sentence that describes your site’s purpose or audience. For example: \";i:6;s:48:\"“Simple budgeting tools for everyday people”\";i:7;s:59:\"“Home workouts and fitness tips that fit your schedule”\";i:8;s:85:\"Keep it short, specific, and friendly. You can change it from the WordPress settings.\";i:9;s:112:\"Set the site tagline on <a href=\"https://nmatondo.42.fr/wp-admin/options-general.php\">General settings page</a>.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:46:\"Site tagline is not set in WordPress settings.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}s:11:\"auth_status\";a:8:{s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:10:\"not_locked\";b:1;s:12:\"button_label\";s:11:\"Connect Now\";s:10:\"button_url\";s:71:\"https://nmatondo.42.fr/wp-admin/admin.php?page=surerank#/search-console\";s:6:\"status\";s:10:\"suggestion\";s:11:\"description\";a:6:{i:0;s:201:\"Google Search Console is a free tool that shows how your site is doing in Google search — how many people are finding it, what they’re searching for, and which pages are getting the most attention.\";i:1;s:230:\"Connecting Search Console to your site doesn’t change anything on the front end — but it gives you a behind-the-scenes view of what’s working. SureRank uses this connection to show useful insights directly in your dashboard.\";i:2;s:26:\"<h6> Why it matters: </h6>\";i:3;s:252:\"Without <a href=\'https://nmatondo.42.fr/wp-admin/admin.php?page=surerank#/search-console\'>Search Console</a>, you\'re flying blind. With it, you get a clear picture of your visibility, clicks, and search appearance — so you can make smarter decisions.\";i:4;s:27:\"<h6> What you can do: </h6>\";i:5;s:303:\"If you haven’t already, set up Google Search Console and connect it in the <a href=\'https://nmatondo.42.fr/wp-admin/admin.php?page=surerank#/search-console\'>SureRank Search Console</a>. It only takes a minute, and once connected, you’ll start seeing real data about how your site is doing in search.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:39:\"Google Search Console is not connected.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}}s:8:\"settings\";a:3:{s:8:\"sitemaps\";a:5:{s:6:\"exists\";b:0;s:6:\"status\";s:7:\"warning\";s:11:\"description\";a:15:{i:0;s:125:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/sitemap-banner.webp\' alt=\'Sitemap example\' />\";i:1;s:18:\"<h6> Sitemap </h6>\";i:2;s:394:\"A sitemap is like a guide or floor plan for your website that helps search engines explore it efficiently. It lists your important pages and shows search engines the path to follow, making sure nothing essential gets missed. Think of it as a chapter list in a book — it doesn’t change how your site looks to visitors, but it helps search engines understand your content quickly and clearly.\";i:3;s:32:\"<h6>💡 Why this matters: </h6>\";i:4;s:127:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/sitemap-example.webp\' alt=\'why this matters\' />\";i:5;s:334:\"Without a sitemap, search engines might overlook some pages or take longer to notice updates. This can slow down how quickly your new content appears in search results. A well-maintained sitemap gives search engines a clear overview of your site, helping your content get indexed faster and more accurately, which improves visibility.\";i:6;s:309:\"Think of it like this: if your website was a story, the sitemap would be the chapter list — helping Google and other search engines jump to the right sections. It doesn’t change how your site looks to visitors, but it makes a big difference in how your site is discovered and understood behind the scenes.\";i:7;s:39:\"<h6>✅ How to keep things smooth </h6>\";i:8;a:1:{s:4:\"list\";a:4:{i:0;s:85:\"Make sure your sitemap is active and accessible by visiting yoursite.com/sitemap.xml.\";i:1;s:94:\"Even if it looks technical, having a list of your pages means search engines know where to go.\";i:2;s:76:\"Keep the sitemap up to date whenever you add new pages or make major changes\";i:3;s:88:\"Use the built-in sitemap management in SureRank to create and maintain it automatically.\";}}i:9;s:22:\"<h6>📌 Example </h6>\";i:10;s:215:\"If you add a new blog post but don’t have a sitemap, search engines might take longer to find it. With a sitemap, your new post appears in search results more quickly, helping readers discover your content sooner.\";i:11;s:36:\"<h6>🛠️ Where to update it </h6>\";i:12;s:107:\"You can manage and update your sitemap directly from the SureRank settings using the built-in sitemap tool.\";i:13;s:33:\"<h6>🌟 How SureRank helps </h6>\";i:14;s:244:\"SureRank automatically generates and updates your sitemap, so search engines always have a clear path to your important content. This keeps your site organized and ensures nothing valuable gets overlooked, without requiring extra work from you.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:48:\"XML sitemap is not accessible to search engines.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}s:12:\"index_status\";a:5:{s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:6:\"status\";s:7:\"success\";s:11:\"description\";a:2:{i:0;s:203:\"Search engine visibility settings need to be enabled. The “Discourage search engines from indexing this site” option in WordPress settings must remain unchecked to allow normal crawling and indexing.\";i:1;s:134:\"Set the search engine visibility on <a href=\"https://nmatondo.42.fr/wp-admin/options-reading.php\">WordPress Reading settings page</a>.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:62:\"Search engine visibility is not blocked in WordPress settings.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}s:10:\"robots_txt\";a:5:{s:6:\"exists\";b:0;s:6:\"status\";s:7:\"warning\";s:11:\"description\";a:15:{i:0;s:129:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/robots.txt-check-banner.webp\' alt=\'Robots.txt\' />\";i:1;s:26:\"<h6> Robots.txt File </h6>\";i:2;s:255:\"Your site has a small file called robots.txt that acts like a guide for search engines, showing them where they’re welcome to explore and where they should stay away. Think of it as a polite set of instructions for visitors who want to browse your site.\";i:3;s:32:\"<h6>💡 Why this matters: </h6>\";i:4;s:138:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/robots.txt-sub-banner.webp\' alt=\'Robots.txt sub banner\' />\";i:5;s:295:\"If the robots.txt file is missing or set up incorrectly, search engines might skip pages they should see, or spend time on pages that aren’t important. A proper file helps your site get noticed efficiently and ensures the content that matters most is visible to both search engines and people.\";i:6;s:39:\"<h6>✅ How to keep things smooth </h6>\";i:7;a:1:{s:4:\"list\";a:4:{i:0;s:103:\"Check your robots.txt by visiting yoursite.com/robots.txt , if it opens with some rules, it’s active.\";i:1;s:61:\"Make sure it doesn’t block pages you want visitors to find.\";i:2;s:82:\"Even if the rules look complicated, having the file is better than not having one.\";i:3;s:81:\"Use the built-in robots.txt editor in SureRank to view or adjust the file safely.\";}}i:8;s:22:\"<h6>📌 Example </h6>\";i:9;s:127:\"<img class=\'w-full h-full\' src=\'https://surerank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/robot-example.webp\' alt=\'Robots.txt example\' />\";i:10;s:185:\"If your robots.txt accidentally blocks your “Shop” or “Pricing” pages, search engines won’t see them, and people searching for your products or services might never find them.\";i:11;s:36:\"<h6>🛠️ Where to update it </h6>\";i:12;s:96:\"The robots.txt file can be edited directly from the SureRank settings using the built-in editor.\";i:13;s:33:\"<h6>🌟 How SureRank helps </h6>\";i:14;s:206:\"SureRank automatically creates a working robots.txt file and lets you manage it directly within the plugin. This keeps your site clear for search engines and ensures important pages are always discoverable.\";}s:7:\"message\";s:34:\"Robots.txt file is not accessible.\";s:6:\"ignore\";b:0;}}}','off'),
